WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.130
GIBRALTAR AIRSPACE

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.830
"Gibraltar Airspace".
GIBRALTAR AIRSPACE

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:25.700
GIBRALTAR AIRSPACE

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.030
BESPA has come to Arti Gibraltar, too?

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.700
You mean they picked up our movements?

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.360
It doesn't seem like it.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.000
They must have planned to come on their own.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.700
Marbet, we're headed out, but hide the machines.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:01.730
Right. It doesn't look like anyone comes here. Go ahead.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.700
Thanks.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.560
Calling Arti Gibraltar Airport.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.730
This is Commander Fuala Griffon,

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.360
commander of the Zanscare Empire's Yellow Jackets.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.960
We will now be landing.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.430
So, is this an armed invasion?

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.100
Not at all.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.360
She may be my superior, but I heard nothing of the sort.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.800
Because, if it was an armed invasion,

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:31.100
Zanscare would be declaring itself the enemy of all mankind.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.700
Mr. Mandella, I'm sure you've already...

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.560
...received notice from Largaine base.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.830
So, why aren't you allowing our forces to occupy Arti Gibraltar?

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.530
Because our corporation is not on any government's side.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.500
Could you please modify that policy?

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:51.430
Did the control tower clear them to land?

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.500
Taxi!

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.360
Ltjg. Cronicle, here are two tickets for the next shuttle.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.230
I'll let you and your girlfriend waiting at the hotel...

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.800
...take a trip into space.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.230
Trying to separate me from the commander.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.860
He's a sly fox.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.830
And what's the little fox doing here, too?!

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.260
No doubt about it. It's the boy I met in Kasarelia.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.400
Katejina's...

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.600
What's happened to Miss Katejina?

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.830
She's free to do as she wishes.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.130
Where is she?

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.030
I don't know. What are you doing here?

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.930
That's my business.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.560
Üso, let's go.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.360
Okay!

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.960
Excuse me. Till next time.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.130
Oh, there's no mistaking it!

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.730
So, you're Üso Ewin.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.960
You look just like Hangerg.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.230
I was shocked when I got word that Myra Miggelle had given birth!

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.200
I see... So, this is the boy you've become.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.830
I still can't believe those two had a child!

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:23.130
So, you don't know where they are now?

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:27.360
I had my people investigate after you called.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.960
When Zanscare began their armed invasion,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.800
your parents returned, but then vanished.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.100
Vanished?

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:39.730
Yes. They rode the rail of the mass driver here...

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.360
...and went into space.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:45.700
Even though they had you around.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.060
I see...

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.500
They went into space.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.600
Üso wouldn't destroy the mass driver's rail, right?

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:01.660
If that happened...

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:06.160
The League Militaire resistance movement would stop dead.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.600
Excuse me, old man.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:14.130
The problem right now is that we're flying planes with PCST markings.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.660
Which is illegal.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.360
The thing is, Lieutenant,

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.730
the Federation hasn't done anything about it so far, right?

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:25.060
I know, which is why I'm even here with you all.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.960
Besides, I kinda like that Üso kid and the Shrike Team gals.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.160
What about me?

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:33.600
Maybe if you didn't have such a smart mouth.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.160
Look, a bridge.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:43.160
Your mother left tickets with me for you. Two of them.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.160
From my mother?

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:49.700
She knew you'd come here with a comrade, and prepared tickets.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.700
You're not going to grant my request, are you?

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:53.900
I can't.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.330
The corporation cannot have contact...

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.400
...with either the Federation or the resistance.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.500
Then why are you letting them...

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.700
...use mobile suits and a mobile armor here?

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:05.560
What?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.800
We just saw them earlier!

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.300
Really?

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:11.460
Mr. Mandella!

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.900
Our guests are leaving. See them off.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:15.630
Yes, sir!

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.400
I've recalled the Tomliats.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.660
I'm sure the corporation will get the message.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:23.330
You're really going to have Lee's unit threaten them?

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.060
Of course. We have a force waiting nearby.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.160
It's too soon to threaten them with force!

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.430
We've wasted too much time.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:35.430
The longer we drag it out, the worse it looks for us and you, Lieutenant.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:36.900
But...

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.400
Please withdraw. You can't see Mandella Soone.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:41.360
Leave at once-

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.600
I politely requested a meeting with him!

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.160
What's that?

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:51.330
They're painted with PCST markings,

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:54.160
but they're League Militaire planes headed south!

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:58.460
So, the corporation's joined with the League Militaire?!

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.230
N-No, we haven't!

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.060
You insult us!

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:06.330
Metchet, order Lee's unit into action. We'll threaten them!

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:06.800
Ma'am!

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:09.400
It's a misunderstanding! Our company would never do this!

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:14.430
Then blow up those transports this instant!

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:23.460
So much for your corporation's neutrality!

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:34.830
Gomez and the others have arrived!

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:35.800
Now what?!

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.230
So, the Frying Pan is here!

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:47.500
We'll take care of those transports.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:49.760
That man was from the Yellow Jackets?

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.200
Wait, please! Not that!

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:52.430
Right... No!

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.800
That's...

00:07:58.260 --> 00:07:59.160
That boy...

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.760
If the corporation has joined with the League Militaire, then...

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:02.300
Wait!

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:03.800
You! You...

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.860
I knew I'd seen you somewhere before!

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:08.560
At the pub.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:13.160
No! You're the one who sent Count Oi Nyung to the guillotine!

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:14.730
K-Kid!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.860
Kwan Lee is en route!

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.860
Where do they think they are?!

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:24.900
Don't touch this child!

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:25.860
Commander!

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.660
The transports may be painted with company markings,

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:33.160
but they're the Federation Forces! They have nothing to do with us!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.130
An obvious lie!

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.330
Mr. Oliver! Üso!

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:36.200
Stay away!

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.960
T-The lady who gave me the chocolate cream...

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.400
Chocolate cream?

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:47.160
You're one of BESPA's Yellow Jackets?

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.700
You tricked us!

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:49.960
Stop it, Odelo!

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:54.700
We're ready for takeoff. Whoever moves, gets shot!

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:57.560
Stop! Don't use weapons here!

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.130
I'm prepared to shoot you and those kids!

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:03.700
Mandella Soone!

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:06.260
We're going to destroy the transports and those mobile suits.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.830
Neutral ground has to be kept clean, after all.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.160
Neither BESPA nor the League Militaire...

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.860
...has the right to break in here!

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:15.900
Shut up!

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:17.230
Mr. Mandella!

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.130
Everyone, run!

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.330
Odelo, take care of Suzy and the others.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.060
Right!

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.230
Mr. Oliver!

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:24.900
Üso, get to Marbet!

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:25.860
Right!

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:37.360
Mahalia! Don't carry any weapons!

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:41.960
If we fight on neutral ground, we lose no matter what!

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:44.300
Keep your rifle on your back! Protect the transports!

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:47.730
Tell Odelo and the others to hide in the airport sublevels!

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:51.500
Sorry, but can you get me to the core fighter?

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.730
Mahalia, take the kid.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.160
Roger! Come here, kid!

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.360
I can just ride in the Gun EZ's hand-

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:08.530
Here we go!

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.700
R-Right...

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:14.030
Are they waiting for reinforcements?

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.030
Yeah, it looks like it.

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:20.700
If you fight here...

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:23.530
We won't start it! Marbet!

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:29.630
Grab on!

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.230
Did you find out about your parents?

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:49.600
Please follow Marbet's fighter.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:52.160
Is that Oliver dangling off of it?

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:53.160
Yeah...

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:12.330
You're lucky. You've got parents to look for.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:15.960
Huh? But, I don't have a clue where they are.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:19.830
Maybe, but it's nice to just think about them.

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:24.600
When I was seven years old, my little brother and my parents...

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:27.660
...were killed in an accident right in front of me.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:34.530
There?

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:35.730
Y-Yeah.

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:47.730
Thank you very much, Miss Mahalia!

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.800
Stay faithful to your folks!

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:51.830
Miss Mahalia...

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:58.560
Mr. Oliver!

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:02.000
If Miss Guillotine attacks, I'm fighting back!

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:05.030
I don't think they really want to fight here, either.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.660
Understood.

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.400
But if shooting starts,

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:12.300
we fight to keep them as far from the mass driver's rail as possible!

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.900
That rail absolutely must not be destroyed!

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:16.000
Understood!

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:21.830
Your father was brilliant when he worked for the corporation...

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:23.900
...as a soldier.

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.730
Is it right for a soldier to abandon his child?

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:29.500
Üso Ewin, here I go!

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:35.200
Mr. Oliver, please send the Boots!

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:36.830
Right, leave it to me.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:50.730
This is what we can't damage?

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:54.300
When people were forced into space colonization,

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.060
it transported what belongings they had left into space.

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:01.400
This is a historic monument that's still doing its transport job.

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.430
It shouldn't be destroyed.

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:12.360
A formation of new models, headed for Gibraltar airport!

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:21.760
Here they come, Sis.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:25.160
Whatever happens, we don't shoot first!

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:26.030
Gotcha.

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:30.000
Who cleared you to enter?! Out! Get out!

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:32.400
We still have some fuel left.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:35.700
If we get hit, the whole airport will go up in flames!

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:40.060
The hangar is a corporation facility, but it may still get bombed.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:40.730
Right.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:44.000
It might be better to go into a corporation building.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:49.000
Well? What are the League Militaire and that Federation transport doing?

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:51.760
Wait, please. See how that mobile suit is moving?

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:54.630
If it brings out its rifle...

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:56.100
Then we win.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:57.830
Should we have Lee try to bait it?

00:13:57.860 --> 00:13:58.560
Do it!

00:13:58.600 --> 00:13:59.500
Yes, ma'am!

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:06.960
Helen, the ones who killed you are here.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.230
And they're trying to stir us up.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:16.530
Helen!

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:22.960
I'll make sure you're avenged, Helen!

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.260
Stop it, Mahalia!

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:26.300
Lower the rifle!

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:31.500
We did it! With this image as proof...

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.600
We've got our excuse!

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:36.060
Avoid damaging the corporation's facilities!

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:38.200
Commence armed suppression!

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:04.260
Sis, they're trying to hit the corporation's facilities!

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:08.360
We have to figure out how far they're willing to go, Mahalia!

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.360
I know.

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:15.130
Haro! Flanders!

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:16.930
Be ready to move at anytime!

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.030
The attack's over!

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:22.130
We'll engage the mobile suits with Lupe Cineau's force!

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:22.860
What?

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.860
I'm taking my vengeance for Helen!

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:36.760
Now fall!

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.760
I won't die so easily!

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.600
Sorry, Cony.

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:47.700
Mahalia and the others are moving toward the rail?

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:56.560
No fair, using the rail as a shield!

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:06.300
A unit that can fire long-range beams?

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:11.860
Metchet, we're being targeted!

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:17.930
Out of my way!

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.900
No good. The rail's in the way.

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:29.960
I can't take it out without causing an explosion!

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.930
You shouldn't get too cocky...

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:37.200
...with that civilian-designed mobile suit!

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:38.230
Dammit!

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:44.860
This power!

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:53.130
Don't try to stop me from finding my parents!

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:57.600
What's happening?

00:16:57.630 --> 00:17:00.500
The pilot's spirit feels even stronger now!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:04.060
Out of the way! Out of the way! Get out of my way!

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:07.260
Üso! He's in too deep!

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:18.160
Is Lupe Cineau so easily beaten? By a single mobile suit?

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:25.230
I have no sympathy for whoever gets in my way!

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:26.400
Where's the Frying Pan?

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:29.300
Miss Marbet?

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:32.060
I've gotta try to avoid a worst-case scenario, here!

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:49.430
Aim for enemy units disengaged from close-quarters combat.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.400
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:50.430 --> 00:17:52.830
He's also got the rail behind him.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.660
I know!

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:56.600
Attack without blowing up the rail!

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:57.200
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:58.260
Incoming from above!

00:17:58.300 --> 00:17:59.060
What?

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:03.000
From the silhouette, it could be the Gundam replica.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:03.660
Metchet!

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:04.300
Sir!

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:08.560
Everyone's engaged in close combat, but there's a single mobile suit...

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.660
...that's acting independently? How amateurish!

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:14.500
Amateurish? It might be that boy!

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:18.100
Boy? Do you mean...

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:22.260
That Üso. It's just the sort of thing he'd pull off! That!

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:24.860
That boy is a pilot?!

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:32.100
I only met him for a few minutes.

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:35.260
If that boy is the white one's pilot, then...

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:40.660
He's the reason for all my failures since Uwig that forced me to use the guillotine?

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:42.630
Kill him, Metchet!

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:45.330
I missed!

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:48.560
Is the lady who seemed so nice really in that thing?!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.000
You missed! I won't keep falling for the same trick!

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:56.960
Metchet, destroy him!

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:57.700
Yes, ma'am!

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:07.560
Their specialty is fighting over water. I can't engage them in the air!

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:13.800
Using the rail as a shield?

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:17.260
You lost him?

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:21.630
Which comes out first, the ogre or the serpent?

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:25.630
There they are!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.100
He was in the tunnel?!

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:46.100
You're crazy, trying to use war to change the world!

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.430
Gundam!

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:53.800
There are people inside!

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:04.100
I can't a shoot someone when I can see their face!

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:05.460
They're going to get me!

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.430
Just fall, already!

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:19.330
Not quite!

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:38.930
Whose Gun EZ was it? Whose...

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:43.500
I couldn't help her!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:49.360
In a war between machines,

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:51.460
they showed me their flesh and blood!

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:53.130
It's not right!

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:58.000
Six Yellow Jacket units, downed.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.330
And us?

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:01.130
Mahalia.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:03.560
Mahalia was...

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.260
I'll go retrieve her.

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:17.360
Üso's machine is back! Üso!

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:19.360
You're not hurt, are you?

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:21.030
Thanks. I'm okay.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.260
What's wrong? You're not going?

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:26.800
It looks like he's got something else bothering him.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.330
It's Mahalia's suit.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.860
Stay faithful to your folks!

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:58.930
Miss Mahalia! Miss Mahalia!

00:22:01.430 --> 00:22:03.200
Miss Mahalia!

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:39.030
BESPA has finally begun its all-out attack.

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:43.030
A battle both above and below the shuttle that Miss Katejina is on.

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:49.900
And on the battlefield, Üso hears Miss Kite's scream.

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:53.760
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:54.400
Next Episode THE BATTLE OF GIBRALTAR

00:23:54.400 --> 00:23:56.730
"The Battle of Gibraltar".

00:23:56.730 --> 00:23:56.760
Next Episode THE BATTLE OF GIBRALTAR

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:58.060
Please watch it!
